    "body": "The failed Context/Cue endpoint improves source competition while leaving a later source-fragment error. This records one saved-only diagnostic of existing Prefix distinctions, fixed U margins and global shared-coefficient tradeoffs across the original eighteen frames. No serving code, model, encoder, gradient, native reducer or proposal runs.\n\nThe helper authenticates190 physical-pair contrasts/460 shared keys (26 opposed), fractional and packed Prefix coefficients, and eighteen already-weighted Cue gradients against95 accepted actual fractional displacements. Both named pairs still have negative raw Copy gaps after the best single adjacent change; wider independent legal boxes have room, but simultaneous shared-key/nonlinear full-pool feasibility remains UNRESOLVED.\n\nThe narrower next question uses the ORIGINAL selected parent for Prefix-only learning of task245 position4target267, absent from the older89-term task objective. The task direct gap is unchanged in the joint negative, which adds a reference regression. That negative remains preserved and unselected. Final acceptance remains original CE descent/exact task probability/all17 winners; actual pooled267 win must separately precede a fragment-correction claim. Prefix compute remains NOT_ADMITTED until prospective policy, source checks and reviews.\n\nValidation: source math/adversarial and saved-result reviews PASS; actual once-only diagnostic10.963725s/peakRSS81492KiB; existing Rust exclusive claim/seal/complete-file verify PASS. Helperf1423815, result93fddcc2/actual Rust manifestd610639b. Runtime517f25ae92ecae617825be14b1cbf9135ea43cf5 and full result3af2dccd12db11830dd7ff01c09b6f66d7eecdc0 freshly downloaded/hash verified. Exacthead ec6822ea04855ce8f563618ae7078c46fb0fec0e JSON/result projection, claim-wording, diff and self review PASS (owner permits self review). No repository Rust path changes; historical CI acknowledgement names execute no tests. Full preparation/review/preservation/delivery charge remains on #820, all new work pod-only and other labs preserved.\n\nReferences #820.",
